    {
      "body": "Found it \u2014 the `flare_Dataset(...)` cell itself raised a `MergeError`, so `train_dataset` was never assigned. That's why every later cell throws `NameError: name 'train_dataset' is not defined` \u2014 it's a downstream symptom, not the real problem.\n\nThe real error:\n```\nMergeError: incompatible merge keys [0] dtype('float64') and dtype('<M8[ns]'), must be the same type\n```\n\nIt happens in `flare_dataset.py:84`, in `pd.merge_asof(self.df_valid_indices, self.ds_index, ...)` \u2014 `df_valid_indices[\"valid_indices\"]` is `float64` while `self.ds_index[\"ds_index\"]` is `datetime64[ns]`. Let me check `flare_dataset.py` to see why `valid_indices` isn't a datetime.",
      "mentions": [],
      "id": "d78725c6-8918-4549-9f29-710a3097fa13",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789565351.5660489,
      "type": "msg"
    },
