    {
      "time": 1789565390.3418381,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "id": "05079fbb-1d60-42b8-b32d-2b03f6fb93fc",
      "body": "That confirms it: an empty `self.valid_indices` list produces a `float64` column, which then can't merge against the `datetime64` `ds_index` column \u2014 that's the `MergeError`. So the root cause is one level up: `HelioNetCDFDataset._filter_valid_indices()` returned zero valid timestamps for this config. Let's check why.",
      "type": "msg",
      "mentions": []
    },
    {
      "mentions": [],
      "id": "3a5dd926-0242-4259-8885-a0d12445e248",
